From 3cb9490302cf72aa0b4cebde6e9c8e9a3cb1b740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saverio Moscardini <4923627+savemosca@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:28:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Android: re-initialise the sensor subsystem for each game
 session

HostWindow::open() initialises SDL_INIT_SENSOR once per process and it
is never quit. On Android the process outlives a game session (a
launcher Activity keeps it), but SDL's sensor driver binds its event
queues to the ALooper of the thread that initialised the subsystem:
the first session's game thread, which ends with that session. In every
later session SDL_SensorOpen / SDL_SensorClose went through the dead
thread's looper and crashed the process, at open or at close:

  SIGSEGV fault addr 0x8      Looper::addFd    <- ASensorManager_createEventQueue
                              <- SDL_SensorOpen  <- HostWindow::open()
  SIGSEGV fault addr 0x3a0    Looper::removeFd <- ASensorManager_destroyEventQueue
                              <- SDL_SensorClose <- HostWindow::close()

Quit the sensor subsystem in close() on Android, after the gyro is
closed, so the next session's open() initialises it on its own thread.
Seen on an Anbernic RG556 (Android 14): the second game started from
the same launcher process crashed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/host_window.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/runtime/host_window.cpp b/src/runtime/host_window.cpp
index b2573a8..0090609 100644
--- a/src/runtime/host_window.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/host_window.cpp
@@ -2298,6 +2298,16 @@ void HostWindow::close() {
     if (b->audio_mtx) SDL_DestroyMutex(b->audio_mtx);
     close_game_controller(b);
     if (b->device_gyro) SDL_SensorClose(b->device_gyro);
+#if defined(__ANDROID__)
+    // The process outlives a game session (a launcher Activity can keep it),
+    // but SDL's Android sensor driver binds every event queue to the ALooper
+    // of the thread that initialised the subsystem: this session's game
+    // thread, which ends with it. Quit the subsystem so the next session's
+    // open() initialises it again on its own thread. Otherwise the next
+    // session's SDL_SensorOpen/SDL_SensorClose went through the dead thread's
+    // looper and crashed in Looper::addFd / Looper::removeFd.
+    SDL_QuitSubSystem(SDL_INIT_SENSOR);
+#endif
     if (b->haptic) SDL_HapticClose(b->haptic);
     if (g_haptic_window == this) g_haptic_window = nullptr;
 #if defined(GBARECOMP_RUNTIME_UI)
